RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE
Office of City Clerk
April 23, 2012
The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne met in regular session on this date beginning
at 6:00 p.m. in Council Chambers.  Present were: MAYOR - Richard L. Kaysen; COUNCIL
MEMBERS - Mr. Allen, Ms. Ash, Mr. Brown, Ms. Broyles, Mr. Collins, Mr. Pierson, Dr. Rinne,
Mr. Spiker and Mr. Valdez.  Also present: Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk; Lois Huff, City Treasurer,
and Dan White, City Attorney.  The pledge of allegiance was recited.
Consent Agenda. (All agenda items listed with the designation of [CA] are considered to be
routine items by the governing body and will be enacted by one motion.  There will be no separate
discussion on these items unless a member of the governing body so requests and support by two
other members is received.  Any item removed from the Consent Agenda will be considered in its
normal sequence on the agenda.)  Mr. Brown moved to approve Consent Agenda items, seconded
by Mr. Allen.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body.
[CA]
Minutes from Regular Meeting of the Governing Body on April 9, 2012. Motion (per
Consent Agenda) carried.
Mr. Valdez moved to approve payment of vouchers as presented, seconded by Mr. Allen.
Upon inquiry, Rick Parish, Parks and Recreation Director, reviewed a voucher payable to Art
Casting of Colorado relating to services to recast a bronze statue located in Lions Park that had been
vandalized.  He stated Arts in Public Places budgeted funds are being utilized as the amount is under
the City’s insurance deductible amount.  Brief comments were made regarding concerns with
vandalism and resulting costs.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body.
An Ordinance amending the City of Cheyenne’s Sanitation Fee Schedule -- referred to
Finance Committee (sponsors -- Mr. Brown and Mr. Collins).
[CA]
Resolution approving the City of Cheyenne=s 2012- 2013 Annual Action Plan prepared by
the Cheyenne Housing and Community Development Office.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried.
(#5376)
Resolution authorizing the Mayor and the City Clerk to sign a Final Plat for North Cheyenne
Community Park, Second Filing, a replat of North Cheyenne Community Park, Cheyenne, Wyoming
(located north of and adjacent to Storey Boulevard, east of and adjacent to Chief Washakie Avenue).
Reporting for Public Services Committee, Ms. Ash moved to adopt with staff recommendations #1
and 2, seconded by Ms. Broyles.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing
body. (#5377)
[CA]
Resolution authorizing an amended Final Plat to accompany Resolution #5295 B as adopted
by the Governing Body on July 11, 2011 for Niobrara Energy Park, a replat of a portion of Tracts
6, 17, & 18, Clear View Tracts, a portion of C.B.C. Subdivison, and a portion of the N2 of Section
9, T.13N., R.66W., 6th P.M., Laramie County, Wyoming (located west of South College Drive
