Application for a Bar and Grill liquor license application filed with the City Clerk’s Office
for Blazin Wings, Inc. d/b/a Buffalo Wild Wings Grill & Bar, 1740 Prairie Avenue, Cheyenne,
Wyoming.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried.
Announcement was made of the Appointment of Howard A. Hill, Sr., to the Mayor’s Council
for People with Disabilities, to be confirmed May 14, 2012.
Announcement was made of a Public Hearing to be held Monday, May 14, 2012 at 6:00 p.m.
in City Council Chambers, 2101 O’Neil Avenue, Cheyenne, Wyoming, to determine whether
compliance of annexation conditions required by Wyo. Stat. §15-1-402 exist for a parcel of land
being situated in a portion of the N½ of the N½ of the NE¼ of the NE¼ of Section 11, T.13N.,
R.67W. of the 6th P.M., Laramie County, Wyoming (generally located at the end of West 5th Street,
west of Southwest Drive, a/k/a 4121 W. 5th Street).
[CA]
Designation of Official Voting Delegate and Alternate Delegate for the City of Cheyenne
at the 2012 Wyoming Association of Municipalities Annual Convention -- referred to Finance
Committee.
Under other business:
Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk, advised there would not be a City Council Public Services
Committee meeting on Tuesday, May 8, 2012 at Noon in Room 122, Municipal Building, as there
were no pending or referred items for the agenda requiring a meeting.
Upon request, Ms. Intlekofer read the following entitlement for an item being introduced
under other business:  “2012-2013 Collective Labor Agreement between the City of Cheyenne,
Wyoming, and Cheyenne Firefighters Local Union No. 279, International Association of
Firefighters” with Mayor Kaysen referring the item to Finance Committee.  It was noted the next
Finance Committee meeting will be held on Monday, May 7, 2012 at 11:00 a.m. in Room 122,
Municipal Building.
Appreciation was expressed to Leadership Cheyenne and Cheyenne Cottonwood Society
